      "role": "user",
      "content": "right, but it's more than just making the room sound better for readers. i noticed the sensors—i mean, the plants—aren't just scattered, they're specifically clustered near the desks where people have private meetings or sensitive research discussions. if you look at the way the aloe leaves are tilted, they act like natural parabolic reflectors. if someone placed a tiny, high-sensitivity transducer or even just a MEMS microphone hidden in the soil or the base of the pot, the plant structure would basically act as a natural amplifier for the voices at the desk. do you think a municipal agency could actually use that setup to monitor conversations without anyone ever noticing a single piece of electronic equipment?",
